-- Database check - the relational side.
-- Eight tables of the information system for registration, notification and reporting of
-- communicable diseases (Abanos et al., 2023), version 4, in the schema the system uses:
-- the nomenclatures of Ordinance No 21 (Annexes 1, 1a, 2 and 3, as amended in State Gazette
-- No 35 of 14 April 2026), the general practitioners, the patients and the 3003 notices with
-- the criteria ticked for each.
--
-- The data is generated. The notices are not cases of real people and do not describe a real
-- epidemic situation. The names of the general practitioners and of their practices are
-- invented; their middle names and e-mail addresses are left empty. The columns of t_patients
-- that hold personal data in the system - names, national number, e-mail, password, address,
-- postal code, telephones and smoking - are left empty (empty text or 0); only the identifier,
-- the date of birth and the sex are kept, because the archetype instances carry them. The login
-- tables of the system are left out.
